.TH WAVE-UNINSTALL 1 "" "MacWave" "MacWave Manual"

.SH NAME
wave-uninstall \- Uninstall a package version. Several packages can be given at once, separated by commas; a package may carry several @versions, or @all for every installed version. The unversioned link falls back to the highest remaining version, and goes away with the last one.
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B wave uninstall <package>[@<version>[@<version>...]] [, ...] [flags]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Uninstall a package version. Several packages can be given at once,
separated by commas; a package may carry several @versions, or @all for
every installed version. The unversioned link falls back to the highest
remaining version, and goes away with the last one.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-a, \-\-all
Remove every installed version of the package (cannot be combined with
@<version>)
.TP
.B \-\-no\-link
Do not touch the unversioned link (the old name --unlink still works)

.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
wave uninstall jq
wave uninstall ffmpeg@6.1
wave uninstall jq, yq
wave uninstall ffmpeg@6.1@6.0, jq@all
wave uninstall jq -a
.fi
.SH SEE ALSO
wave(1)
